# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  SECRETS — never commit these
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
#  .env.local holds live credentials in this project:
#
#    SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY   bypasses all row-level security. Anyone holding it
#                               has full read/write on every table, including
#                               every customer's address and order.
#    RAZORPAY_KEY_SECRET         signs and verifies payment amounts.
#    GROQ_API_KEY                billed per call.
#
#  Committing it does not merely leak the key, it publishes it — and a
#  service-role key cannot be rotated by deleting the commit history from the
#  server later. Keep it out.
#
#  .env.example IS committed on purpose: it documents the variable names with
#  empty values so a new machine knows what to fill in.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
!.env.example

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Dependencies — reinstallable, and enormous
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js
.yarn/*
!.yarn/patches

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Build output
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Logs
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Tooling caches
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.turbo/
.cache/
.eslintcache
coverage/
*.lcov

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Local database used by the test suites
#
#  scripts/test-schema.mjs and scripts/test-catalogue.mjs spin up an in-process
#  Postgres for their fixtures. It is disposable and often very large.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.pglite/
*.pglite/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  OS / editor noise
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  Keep the generated catalogue and its image sources
#
#  These two look like build artefacts but are deliberately committed: the seed
#  must be reproducible offline, and `npm run seed` reads image-sources.mjs.
#  Nothing under supabase/ or scripts/ is ignored.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────